# Milestone: M5
# Covers: e! (async emit) — event fires all AT_EVENT subscribers in registration
#         order; subscriber bodies run asynchronously on spawned coroutines.
#
# blocked: spawn_body_coroutine path for at(e?) subscriber dispatch — body fires once on emit but logging slot-write ordering not yet observable (audit Cat. E)
# matrix-row: reactive-event
#
# Reason:
#   Event.new() requires T59 stdlib binding (attaches Event prototype to realm
#   globals via urbi_populate_realm_globals).  The at (e?) subscribe watcher
#   uses OP_AT_EVENT_INSTALL (T47), which is wired.  The subscriber body
#   dispatch requires spawn_body_coroutine (stub at M5-stub phase).  The
#   urbi_event_emit_async path is exercised by test_event_emit_async.c.
#
# Activate when Event.new() + scratch-frame body dispatch are wired.
#
# Urbiscript source (activate at T59 + M5-scratch-frame):
#   var e = Event.new();
#   var log = "";
#   at (e?) Realm.log = Realm.log + "A";
#   at (e?) Realm.log = Realm.log + "B";
#   e!;
#   log
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000000] nil
#   [00000001] ""
#   [00000002] nil
#   [00000003] nil
#   [00000004] nil
#   [00000005] "AB"
